 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nFunction argument default value inference broken\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen inferring values for function arguments with default values, the inference process no longer yields the default value. This affects static analysis tools that rely on astroid to understand what values function parameters might have.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport astroid\n\ncode = \"\"\"\ndef func(x=42):\n    return x\n\nfunc()\n\"\"\"\n\nmodule = astroid.parse(code)\nfunc_def = module.body[0]\ncall_node = module.body[1].value\n\n# Try to infer what the argument 'x' could be\nargs_node = func_def.args\nfor inferred in args_node.infer_argument_value('x', None):\n    print(f\"Inferred value: {inferred}\")\n```\n\nExpected: Should print the default value `42` and possibly `Uninferable`\nActual: Only prints `Uninferable`\n\nThe issue affects any code that tries to understand what values function parameters with defaults might take, which is important for type checking and static analysis.\n</issue>\n",
